CommitDate: Sat Sep 12 20:33:53 2026 +0200

    Fix `pMap` settling early when the source iterator throws with `stopOnError: false`
    
    When the source iterator threw after a mapper had resolved, the in-flight count was decremented twice, so `pMap` could reject with an incomplete `AggregateError` while mappers were still running. Errors from the source iterator now always reject immediately, matching the existing behavior when the iterator throws after a mapper error.

diff --git a/index.js b/index.js
